From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xorbidden <xorbidden@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:01:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] torch: support the PM6150L's flash LED module

The driver knew only the PM8350C's flash module (peripheral 0x2ee, one
torch channel). The PM6150L's (0x5d3, the Mi 9T's) lights two channels
at once and has other register offsets, safety-timer encoding, current
resolution and fault bits (leds-qpnp-flash-v2.c of the sm6150 kernel).

- Put the registers that differ into a struct layout, one per PMIC.
- Pick the module with boot-arg pmic_flash= (default 0x2ee, as before);
  the layout follows from it. Unknown ids are refused.
- Write each channel's safety timer, target current and strobe for
  every channel the torch lights.
Upstream's recent safety fixes (dark() forcing its writes past the
`broken' latch, `lit' set before the enabling writes) are kept.

Not yet built in this layout; the logic ran on the Mi 9T in the old
port (torch=3 from Control Center).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
